    <activity>
        <p>
            <term>Work in Groups</term>
        </p>

        <p>
            For each of the following numbers:
        </p>
        <p>
            <ol marker="(a)">
                <li>
                    <p>
                        Round off to the stated number of significant figures.
                    </p>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <p>
                        Truncate to the stated number of significant figures.
                    </p>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <p>
                        Calculate the percentage error in each case.
                    </p>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <p>
                        State which method gives the more accurate approximation.
                    </p>
                </li>
            </ol>
        </p>
        <p>
            Use:
        </p>
        <p>
            <md>
                \text{Percentage Error}=
                \frac{|\text{True Value}-\text{Approximate Value}|}
                {\text{True Value}}
                \times100\%
            </md>
        </p>
        <p>
            <ol marker="(i)">
                <li>
                    <m>48.769</m> correct to <m>3</m> significant figures.
                </li>

                <li>
                    <m>0.0047865</m> correct to <m>2</m> significant figures.
                </li>

                <li>
                    <m>3958</m> correct to <m>2</m> significant figures.
                </li>

                <li>
                    <m>126.498</m> correct to <m>4</m> significant figures.
                </li>

                <li>
                    <m>0.99949</m> correct to <m>3</m> significant figures.
                </li>
            </ol>
        </p>
        <p>
            Present your answers and explain your calculations to the class.
        </p>
    </activity>

